---
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="KiduCode Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for KiduCode Cloud and associated integrations, including our Vercel OAuth application."
>
  <section class="section-grid py-16 lg:py-24">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Terms"
      title="Terms of Service"
      description="These Terms of Service govern your use of the KiduCode Cloud and its associated integrations, including our Vercel OAuth application."
      as="h1"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid pb-20">
    <article class="surface-panel rounded-[28px] p-8 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">1. Acceptance of Terms and Cloud Services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">By accessing or using the KiduCode Cloud services, you agree to these Terms of Service. These terms cover both our command-line tools and our hosted Cloud Console.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">2. Authorization to Access Connected Services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">When you connect third-party platforms such as Vercel or GitHub to KiduCode via OAuth, you explicitly authorize us to access, modify, and manage your resources (e.g., deployments, repositories, environment variables) as requested during the authorization flow. You may revoke this access at any time via the respective third-party platform.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">3. User Responsibility for Code and Deployments</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">You are solely responsible for reviewing, testing, and deploying any code generated or modified by KiduCode. While we aim to provide accurate and helpful coding assistance, KiduCode does not guarantee that the generated code is error-free, secure, or fit for any specific purpose. You accept full responsibility for all deployments triggered through our integrations.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">4. AI Output Limitations</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">KiduCode relies on artificial intelligence to generate code and workflow suggestions. AI outputs can occasionally be inaccurate, unpredictable, or produce unintended functionality. You acknowledge these inherent limitations and agree to thoroughly audit any AI-generated modifications before integrating them into production environments.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">5. Third-Party Charges (Vercel and GitHub)</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">KiduCode integrations may automate actions (such as pushing commits or triggering builds) that consume resources on connected third-party services like GitHub or Vercel. You are solely responsible for monitoring your usage on these platforms and for any associated costs, overages, or fees incurred as a result of using KiduCode.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">6. Acceptable Use and Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">You agree not to use KiduCode for any illegal, harmful, or malicious purposes. You retain all intellectual property rights to the code you create and manage using our platform. KiduCode claims no ownership over your proprietary code or the specific outputs generated for your projects.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">7. Availability and Warranty Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">The KiduCode Cloud services are provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. We disclaim all warranties, whether express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We do not guarantee uninterrupted access to the platform or integrations.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">8. Liability Limitations and Governing Law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">To the maximum extent permitted by law, KiduCode and its affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of profits, data, use, or goodwill resulting from your use of the services. These terms shall be governed by the laws of your local jurisdiction, without regard to conflict of law principles.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">9. Account Termination and Data Deletion</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7">We reserve the right to suspend or terminate your access to the KiduCode services at any time for violation of these Terms. You may delete your account at any time. Upon termination or deletion, we will delete all associated OAuth access tokens and metadata in accordance with our Privacy Policy.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
